From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:30:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] v20-common: let the lineage-sdk overlay apply at all

overlay-lineage is added through DEVICE_PACKAGE_OVERLAYS, but msm8996-common sets
PRODUCT_ENFORCE_RRO_TARGETS := * and excludes only its own overlay-lineage/lineage-sdk from RRO
enforcement. lineage-sdk's resource package gets no auto-generated RRO, so this tree's copy was
neither compiled in nor overlaid at runtime. Every value in it was dropped with no diagnostic, for
as long as the file has existed.

Proven against the compiled resources in org.lineageos.platform-res.apk: the overlay asks for
config_cleanupUnusedFingerprints false and the built value is true.

The only value this changes in practice is config_deviceLightCapabilities, from lineage-sdk's
default 8 to 0, which stops advertising LIGHTS_PULSATING_LED on a device with no notification LED.
The other two in the file stay inert: config_haveNotch has no consumer in the tree, and
config_cleanupUnusedFingerprints is read only by the AIDL FingerprintProvider while this device uses
the HIDL fingerprint path.
---
 v20.mk | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/v20.mk b/v20.mk
index 562287d..00a06e1 100644
--- a/v20.mk
+++ b/v20.mk
@@ -30,6 +30,14 @@ PRODUCT_COPY_FILES += \
 DEVICE_PACKAGE_OVERLAYS += $(LOCAL_PATH)/overlay
 DEVICE_PACKAGE_OVERLAYS += $(LOCAL_PATH)/overlay-lineage
 
+# msm8996-common sets PRODUCT_ENFORCE_RRO_TARGETS := *, so every overlay above becomes an
+# auto-generated RRO unless its path is excluded. lineage-sdk's resource package gets no
+# auto-generated RRO, so without this the overlay-lineage values are neither compiled in nor
+# overlaid at runtime: they are dropped, with nothing in the build log. Verify with
+# `aapt2 dump resources .../org.lineageos.platform-res.apk` rather than by reading the overlay.
+PRODUCT_ENFORCE_RRO_EXCLUDED_OVERLAYS += \
+    $(LOCAL_PATH)/overlay-lineage/lineage-sdk
+
 PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
     AvoidAppsInCutoutOverlay
 
